BoTNet by design is simple: replace the final three spatial ($3\times 3$) convolutions in a ResNet with Multi-Head Self-Attention (MHSA) layers that implement global (\emph{all2all}) self-attention over a 2D featuremap (Fig \ref{fig:alephdiagram}). A ResNet typically has 4 stages (or blockgroups) commonly referred to as \texttt{[c2,c3,c4,c5]} with strides \texttt{[4,8,16,32]} relative to the input image, respectively. Stacks \texttt{[c2,c3,c4,c5]} consist of multiple \emph{bottleneck} blocks with residual connections (e.g, R50 has \texttt{[3,4,6,3]} bottleneck blocks).

