\section{Conclusion}
The design of vision backbone architectures that use self-attention is an exciting topic. We hope that our work helps in improving the understanding of architecture design in this space. Incorporating self-attention for other computer vision tasks such as keypoint detection~\cite{cao2017realtime} and 3D shape prediction~\cite{gkioxari2019mesh}; studying self-attention architectures for self-supervised learning in computer vision~\cite{henaff2019data, he2019momentum, tian2019contrastive, chen2020simple, grill2020bootstrap, chen2020exploring}; and scaling to much larger datasets such as JFT, YFCC and Instagram, are ripe avenues for future research. Comparing to, and incorporating alternatives to self-attention such as lambda-layers~\cite{bello2021lambdanetworks} is an important future direction as well.
